it's going to the plaza.

269
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:25,837
It's almost broken through the
bubble protecting the island.

270
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:28,537
Once that thing pops,
we're all goners for sure.

271
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:30,840
We'll be sent to watery graves!

272
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:34,260
Wanna fill me in?

273
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:35,440
It's the Noah!

274
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:39,990
Whoa!

275
00:20:40,073 --> 00:20:41,686
That thing is super gigantic!

276
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:46,357
If that ship hits us, the island
isn't gonna stand a chance!

277
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:48,911
Whoever's operating it needs to pull back!

278
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:49,980
They can't!

279
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:51,749
It doesn't have an engine!

280
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:55,920
There is no way that this will
end well for us! It's okay!

281
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:57,070
This is it!

282
00:20:57,153 --> 00:20:59,000
We're dead for sure this time!

283
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:01,497
In our last moments, I
can't help but wonder,

284
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:04,097
will our blood be enough
to stain the sea red?

285
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:07,037
Can you not say morbid
things like that right now?

286
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:08,860
Let's make a break for it!

287
00:21:09,100 --> 00:21:11,159
Get into the water while you can't!

288
00:21:25,980 --> 00:21:26,810
Wait!

289
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:28,260
Wait, everyone!

290
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:31,380
Look up there!

291
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:52,420
Why do I gotta be so clumsy?

292
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:56,160
That's one of Vander
Decken's men. Watatsumi!

293
00:22:00,340 --> 00:22:02,880
Captain Decken, can you hear me up there?

294
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:06,300
I fell off to knowing I can't get back!

295
00:22:06,740 --> 00:22:08,920
You have to stop that ship for me!

296
00:22:09,540 --> 00:22:11,780
I don't want to die down here!

297
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:14,000
Wait a moment.

298
00:22:14,780 --> 00:22:16,015
Deccan's behind this.

299
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:18,660
Hey, Captain Hardy!

300
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:20,300
Are you okay?

301
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:24,374
Also, I'm curious if this is
a part of your plan, maybe?

302
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:29,300
I mean, it could be because Deccan
is controlling the ship, but...

303
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:32,340
Will you shut up?

304
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:33,440
I'm busy here.

305
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:35,210
Damn you.

306
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:37,640
I'll kill you, Straw Hat. Wow.

307
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,797
I really didn't think you'd
get back up after that one.

308
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:43,056
I guess this guy's no joke after all.

309
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:50,820
Is he out of his mind?

310
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,061
What the hell is Deccan thinking?

311
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:56,105
That bastard is about to
ruin all my hard work!

312
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:18,300
I am offering my love one last time!

313
00:23:29,140 --> 00:23:30,620
Get the dick away!

314
00:23:31,300 --> 00:23:32,720
How do I not die?

315
00:23:35,340 --> 00:23:36,380
Sorry, pal.

316
00:23:37,100 --> 00:23:40,629
You should have thought about
not dying before you fell off.

317
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:42,019
Them's the brakes.

318
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:46,671
You're just one more thing I have to
sacrifice in my pursuit of Shura Hachi.

319
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:47,630
He's out!

320
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:53,040
Why is this happening?

321
00:23:53,460 --> 00:23:55,177
The bubble's about to pop.

322
00:23:55,260 --> 00:23:56,617
We're doomed for sure.

323
00:23:56,700 --> 00:24:00,517
Hey where did princess Shirahoshi go?

324
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:03,357
She vanished this.

325
00:24:03,440 --> 00:24:05,097
Isn't good princess?

326
00:24:05,180 --> 00:24:07,320
Please you have to come back.

327
00:24:09,020 --> 00:24:10,137
What's this?

328
00:24:10,220 --> 00:24:12,037
My Shirahoshi has disappeared.

329
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:14,580
No not now.

330
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:16,620
I'm right here!

331
00:24:20,620 --> 00:24:21,860
Princess Shirahoshi!

332
00:24:22,180 --> 00:24:23,592
When'd she get up there?

333
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:24,980
Please don't die!

334
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:26,520
Come back down!

335
00:24:26,780 --> 00:24:28,377
What do you think you're doing?

336
00:24:28,460 --> 00:24:32,817
She's changing the ship's trajectory
by moving herself away from the island.

337
00:24:32,900 --> 00:24:33,730
What?

338
00:24:33,960 --> 00:24:37,240
Now that's exactly what I'd
expect from my dream girl!

339
00:24:38,100 --> 00:24:39,720
I knew you were awful!

340
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:42,457
But I never believed you
would stoop this low!

341
00:24:42,540 --> 00:24:43,370
No!

342
00:24:43,453 --> 00:24:46,157
If you want to take my life,
then I am powerless to stop you!

343
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:48,377
But no one else should have to suffer!

344
00:24:48,460 --> 00:24:50,460
I won't let you harm this kingdom!

345
00:24:50,580 --> 00:24:52,640
I will protect it with my life!

346
00:24:55,020 --> 00:24:56,940
So come get me, you monster!

347
00:24:58,500 --> 00:24:59,330
Princess!

348
00:25:00,060 --> 00:25:00,890
No!

349
00:25:03,220 --> 00:25:04,050
Figures.

350
00:25:04,133 --> 00:25:06,465
That's what I get for
teaming up with a madman.

351
00:25:06,840 --> 00:25:09,377
I expected he might kill a few commoners,

352
00:25:09,460 --> 00:25:12,048
but now I see he just
as soon killed me too.

353
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:13,910
Hmm.

354
00:25:13,993 --> 00:25:15,660
I won't stand for betrayal.

355
00:25:19,860 --> 00:25:20,690
Please!

356
00:25:20,860 --> 00:25:22,820
Don't sacrifice yourself for us!

357
00:25:23,040 --> 00:25:25,158
We have to do something to save her!

358
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,070
Lovely!

359
00:25:34,153 --> 00:25:36,960
Your beauty is so much
more than skin teeth.

360
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:38,977
Faced with impossible odds,

361
00:25:39,060 --> 00:25:43,060
you take matters into your own hands
to save the countless citizens.

362
00:25:43,260 --> 00:25:45,319
I hope to crash for no good reason.

363
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:46,530
Ah!

364
00:25:47,220 --> 00:25:48,660
You're a whole day!

365
00:25:54,580 --> 00:25:57,080
This is so unfair.

366
00:25:58,140 --> 00:26:02,097
As I always suspected,
you are the perfect woman?

367
00:26:02,180 --> 00:26:03,360
to become Mrs.

368
00:26:03,540 --> 00:26:04,952
Vanderdeck in the ninth.

369
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:09,477
But since you insist on rejecting me,

370
00:26:09,560 --> 00:26:12,420
I fear your beauty must
be resigned to history.

371
00:26:12,860 --> 00:26:13,860
Now die!

372
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:18,720
Please run away!

373
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:28,760
Dammit, weepy Hachi!

374
00:26:29,060 --> 00:26:31,589
I told you to stay
where I can protect you!

375
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:34,080
He's trying to get away!

376
00:26:34,260 --> 00:26:35,400
Captain Horny!

377
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:37,120
What the hell?

378
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:39,301
Where did the captain run off to?

379
00:26:40,700 --> 00:26:41,700
Look up there!

380
00:26:41,860 --> 00:26:43,000
He's on that chain!

381
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:46,080
He's making a break for the Nami!

382
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:02,459
I'll show you what happens
to trainers, Fandertekin.

383
00:27:02,620 --> 00:27:05,500
But I do admit, I like
this idea, of course.

384
00:27:28,080 --> 00:27:28,910
Unforgivable.

385
00:27:28,993 --> 00:27:31,289
I'll make him pay for
hurting the princess.

386
00:27:32,520 --> 00:27:34,620
Saint, hold it! I'll go!

387
00:27:35,080 --> 00:27:37,000
You take care of the plaza!

388
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:38,440
Are you sure?

389
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:41,117
Think about it, Luffy.

390
00:27:41,200 --> 00:27:42,640
The ship's in the water.

391
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:45,777
Put the ship's in a bubble,
so it should be okay.

392
00:27:45,860 --> 00:27:47,154
That would make sense.

393
00:27:47,600 --> 00:27:50,071
Deccan is weak to seawater, just like you.

394
00:27:50,520 --> 00:27:54,108
Despite being a fish man, he
needs air to move around freely.

395
00:27:54,260 --> 00:27:56,084
Better safe than sorry, though.

396
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:58,633
Take this bubbly coral.

397
00:27:59,900 --> 00:28:00,730
Good call.

398
00:28:06,380 --> 00:28:08,497
I can't believe I'm
letting you save the girl.

399
00:28:08,580 --> 00:28:10,200
You better not let us down!

400
00:28:10,380 --> 00:28:12,262
Don't hold anything back, Luffy!

401
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:16,800
Here I go!
